503, 526, and 530, but no definition exists under `src/` or `test/`. Those calls throw, so the suite fails in CI.\n\nImplement the parser field and the helper in `src/ops/dev/coderabbit.ts`. Their behavior must match the expectations in these tests. Otherwise, remove the assertions until the source change lands.","id":"422a4233c416205080cd4337a12cbabaa915a02e80a30c2f65a986e6d6d9345f","intervals":[],"path":"test/ops/dev/coderabbit.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Add the `structuredEvents` field and `deferredVendorErrorCodes` helper, or remove these assertions."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"9f44a1534608010b41394601a91d689a7f4ff470","body":"**Clarify permissions for consuming `review.report` at `docs/queue-client.md:98`.**\n\n`review.report` reads receipt pages, then sends `ack` after import. `ack` requires write permission. A read-only principal can read pages but cannot complete the consuming workflow. The separate read/write authorization is intentional, so document that a consuming reporter must be listed in both allowlists.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested documentation fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-Read covers status/report; write covers enqueue/bind/cancel/ack.\n+Read covers status/report pages; write covers enqueue/bind/cancel/ack. A consuming `review.report` caller must be listed in both `read` and `write`.\n```\n\n</details>","id":"032f09f95f28d29f2cf5a90f066850bebd19cd7a0d4268353970556452912513","intervals":[],"path":"docs/queue-client.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Clarify permissions for consuming `review.report` at `docs/queue-client.md:98`."}],"head":"1de6a353eeec138dcc1e6b766d1350e479902d98","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"e3ec9650f736ef1cd177b5dca49315f046b461da","intervals":[[8,28],[42,42]],"path":"docs/current-contract-and-backlog.md"},{"blob":"41c6e7e7a1799536fe348ab5aeb6719954940b63","intervals":[[1,140]],"path":"d